schc
Copyright 2026 Abhinav Gautam

SCHC header compression and fragmentation, rules in the RFC 9363 data
model, and V.44 compression, in Go.

This module is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE).

The code was written for SigmaM2M from the published specifications listed
in PROVENANCE.md. It contains no code from other projects. Source files
without a per-file copyright header are covered by the copyright line
above; newer files carry "Copyright 2026 Abhinav Gautam" and
"SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0".

Published values and test vectors are used as facts and cited where used;
no specification text is reproduced (see PROVENANCE.md).

Third-party data (not code), from openschc
(https://github.com/openschc/openschc, commit 58293f71), under the MIT
licence, "Copyright (c) 2018 OpenSCHC XXX" and "Copyright (c) 2017-2018
Shoichi Sakane" as its LICENSE states them; the licence text is next to
each file:

- testdata/openschc/schc.json: an example rule set, used as a test input.
- coreconf/sid/ietf-schc@2023-01-28.sid and
  coreconf/sid/ietf-schc-oam@2021-11-10.sid: SID assignments, embedded in
  the coreconf package as its default SIDs.

The interop test module (interop/, not part of the library) builds Docker
images of openschc (MIT, commit 58293f71) and schc-over-sigfox
(https://github.com/schc-over-sigfox/schc-over-sigfox, MIT, commit
1ec0b723, "Copyright (c) 2021 schc-over-sigfox"), fetched at build time
and not redistributed here; the drivers that call them are ours. One
Compound ACK captured from schc-over-sigfox is a test vector in
sigfox_decode_internal_test.go.

Dependencies: the schc and schc/v44 packages use only the Go standard
library. The schc/coreconf package uses github.com/fxamacker/cbor/v2
(MIT), which uses github.com/x448/float16 (MIT).
